# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vl-directory-filename-helpers-fail-macos — BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS fails 2 checks on macOS
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-vl-directory-files-macos-tmp

* Resolution (2026-08-03, alfe/clautolisp master @ c0544de)

Already fixed by commit =069e81d= ("fix(test): vl-directory-files test uses
uiop:temporary-directory (macOS /tmp symlink)"). The test built its scratch
directory from a hard-coded =/tmp/…=; on macOS =/tmp= is a symlink into
=/private=, and listing files through the un-canonicalised symlink path
broke =vl-directory-files='s name comparison, so the first two =is= forms
(=all-names=, =file-names=) failed. Switching the scratch dir to
=uiop:temporary-directory= (the real, canonical temp dir — the same one the
encoding-roundtrip test already used) resolved it; the three list-compare
forms also gained value-carrying description strings for future triage.

Verified: on pipeline 2726349431 the =test:clautolisp:macos= job is GREEN
and =BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS= runs all-dots (no =ff=), 0
failures. Windows + Linux were never affected. Closed as done — no further
work; the "add descriptions / reproduce on macOS" first-step is moot.

* Symptom (original)

On the macOS clautolisp test lane, the FiveAM test
BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS reported two failed checks:

    Running test BUILTIN-VL-DIRECTORY-AND-FILENAME-HELPERS ff...........
    Did 1549 checks.  Fail: 2

The two failing =is= forms carried no description string (=[]=), so the
trace showed only the count. The rest of the test passed.

* Scope / not a regression

- macOS ONLY: test:clautolisp:windows and the Linux suite passed the same test.
- Pre-existing across several pipelines (540f232, 2f151e7, fb38d9a, 0a7aa86 —
  the G2/G3/Phase-4 encoding commits), none of which touch vl-directory /
  vl-filename. The macOS runner is intermittent and had not run for a while,
  so it only surfaced then.
- Unrelated to the encoding work (ENCODING-FILE-ROUNDTRIP and the
  CLAL-FILE-ENCODING-* tests all passed on the same macOS run).

* Likely cause (confirmed)

A macOS-specific path assumption: =/tmp= vs =/private= symlink
canonicalisation in the vl-directory helper test. Fixed as above.
